body:
Components in fumadocs documentation (calendar, buttons, etc.) are rendering without styles due to missing Tailwind v4 theme configuration.

## Problem

After the Tailwind v4 upgrade in PR #158, the fumadocs site was missing the `@theme` directive required for Tailwind v4 to generate utility classes. The site had `@import 'tailwindcss'` but without the `@theme` configuration, no utility classes like `.bg-primary`, `.bg-destructive`, etc. were being generated.

User confirmed this styling issue existed even before the v4 upgrade - the site never had proper Tailwind configuration (neither v3 nor v4).

## Changes

**Added Tailwind v4 theme configuration to `apps/site/app/global.css`:**

```css
@theme {
  /* Border radius tokens */
  --radius-lg: var(--radius);
  --radius-md: calc(var(--radius) - 2px);
  --radius-sm: calc(var(--radius) - 4px);

  /* Color tokens mapped to CSS variables */
  --color-border: hsl(var(--border));
  --color-input: hsl(var(--input));
  --color-ring: hsl(var(--ring));
  --color-background: hsl(var(--background));
  --color-foreground: hsl(var(--foreground));
  --color-primary: hsl(var(--primary));
  --color-primary-foreground: hsl(var(--primary-foreground));
  --color-secondary: hsl(var(--secondary));
  --color-secondary-foreground: hsl(var(--secondary-foreground));
  --color-destructive: hsl(var(--destructive));
  --color-destructive-foreground: hsl(var(--destructive-foreground));
  --color-muted: hsl(var(--muted));
  --color-muted-foreground: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
  --color-accent: hsl(var(--accent));
  --color-accent-foreground: hsl(var(--accent-foreground));
  --color-popover: hsl(var(--popover));
  --color-popover-foreground: hsl(var(--popover-foreground));
  --color-card: hsl(var(--card));
  --color-card-foreground: hsl(var(--card-foreground));
}
```

**Added `tailwindcss-animate` plugin:**
- Added `@plugin 'tailwindcss-animate'` directive
- Installed `tailwindcss-animate` package dependency

**Removed obsolete Tailwind v3 configuration:**
- Deleted `tailwind.config.ts` file (ignored in Tailwind v4)

## Solution

The configuration now matches the working setup in `packages/components/src/index.css`. The key was using `@theme` without the `reference` keyword - using `@theme reference` prevents Tailwind from generating utility classes.

## Status

✅ **Issue Resolved**: Tailwind v4 theme configuration is now properly set up and matches the working components package configuration. Utility classes will be generated correctly.

